            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Roberts, chief Justice Roberts opened the argument by noting the case will be heard."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "cbde50418314d37d6fd98c47d865572f5289bb1770b3130f386daa5391d5b268",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-cbde50418314-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner, petitioner presented arguments seeking reversal of the Ninth Circuit's decision."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "cbde50418314d37d6fd98c47d865572f5289bb1770b3130f386daa5391d5b268",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-cbde50418314-0000-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 13,
              "start": 13
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioner also argued that the State courts made no factual findings."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "United States (amicus)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "cbde50418314d37d6fd98c47d865572f5289bb1770b3130f386daa5391d5b268",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-cbde50418314-0000-0008"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 19,
              "start": 19
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to United States (amicus), the United States, as amicus curiae, presented oral argument supporting the petitioner."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Souter",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "cbde50418314d37d6fd98c47d865572f5289bb1770b3130f386daa5391d5b268",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-cbde50418314-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Souter asked whether any statements about the death penalty had been given to the venire before voir dire."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "cbde50418314d37d6fd98c47d865572f5289bb1770b3130f386daa5391d5b268",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-cbde50418314-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Stevens, justice Stevens questioned a suggestion about Judge Kozinski's basis for his decision."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "cbde50418314d37d6fd98c47d865572f5289bb1770b3130f386daa5391d5b268",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-cbde50418314-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kennedy, justice Kennedy noted that the defense volunteered \"no objection.\""
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "cbde50418314d37d6fd98c47d865572f5289bb1770b3130f386daa5391d5b268",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-cbde50418314-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 22,
              "start": 22
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Breyer, justice Breyer commented that the transcript did not show a word suggesting opposition to the death penalty."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "cbde50418314d37d6fd98c47d865572f5289bb1770b3130f386daa5391d5b268",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-cbde50418314-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 34,
              "start": 34
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Scalia asked why there was no objection if the issue was clear."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Ms. Elliott",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "cbde50418314d37d6fd98c47d865572f5289bb1770b3130f386daa5391d5b268",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-cbde50418314-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Ms. Elliott (respondent) argued about juror excusal and conditions for imposing the death penalty."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "cbde50418314d37d6fd98c47d865572f5289bb1770b3130f386daa5391d5b268",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-cbde50418314-0000-0009"
            ],
